      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first post office, called Four Corners, opened on September 19, 1815, becoming Springville\u2019s first formal institution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/springville_pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers cleared dense beech, maple, and hemlock forests for farmland, then floated lumber down Meshoppen Creek to markets in Harrisburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/springville_pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Springville\u2019s name comes from the many clear springs that feed local creeks, highlighting its well\u2011watered landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/springville_pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A Methodist class formed in 1816 and the Presbyterian Church organized in 1819, underscoring religion\u2019s role in early community life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
